<article class="env-lemma" id="03HU">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03HU">Lemma <span data-tag="03HU">7.25.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a site. Let $U \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. Let $X/U$ be an object of $\mathcal{C}/U$. Then we have $j_{U!}(h_{X/U}^\# ) = h_ X^\# $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Denote $p : X \to U$ the structure morphism of $X$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/03CD" data-tag="03CD">7.25.2</a> we see $j_{U!}(h_{X/U}^\# )$ is the sheaf associated to the presheaf 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  V \longmapsto \coprod \nolimits _{\varphi \in \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {C}(V, U)} \{ \psi : V \to X \mid p \circ \psi = \varphi \}   \]
</div>
    <p>
       This is clearly the same thing as $\mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits _\mathcal {C}(V, X)$. Hence the lemma follows. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>